{"title":"Career Roadmap · CMF Designer","role":"CMF Designer","summary":"A CMF (Color, Material & Finish) Designer develops the visual and tactile character of products and vehicles through color palettes, materials, textures, surface finishes, trims, fabrics, plastics, metals, coatings, and emerging sustainable materials.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Transportation / Automobile Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"In automotive design, CMF sits at the intersection of industrial design, materials science, consumer psychology, manufacturing, branding, and automotive trends."},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Transportation/Automobile Design","CMF Intern","Junior CMF Designer","CMF Designer","Senior CMF Designer","CMF Lead / CMF Design Manager"],"label":"Typical route"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A CMF Designer can work across:"},{"type":"table","header":["Industry","Opportunities"],"rows":[[{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Exterior & Interior CMF"}],[{"text":"Electric Vehicles"},{"text":"EV interior/exterior material strategy"}],[{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Two-wheelers, buses, commercial vehicles"}],[{"text":"Luxury Automotive"},{"text":"Premium materials and finishes"}],[{"text":"Consumer Electronics"},{"text":"Phones, laptops, wearables"}],[{"text":"Furniture"},{"text":"Materials and surface finishes"}],[{"text":"Lifestyle Products"},{"text":"Accessories and premium goods"}],[{"text":"Aviation"},{"text":"Aircraft interiors"}],[{"text":"Marine"},{"text":"Yacht and boat interiors"}],[{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"Material and finish consultancy"}],[{"text":"Wearables"},{"text":"Textiles, polymers and coatings"}],[{"text":"Sustainable Design"},{"text":"Bio-materials and recycled materials"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"The automobile industry is the most direct route for this degree specialization."